    "en": "Hong Kong — delivery infrastructure. AFSC describes 12 on-airport tanks with 220,000 m³ of installed capacity, an apron hydrant network and the Sha Chau marine facility as emergency backup to the permanent aviation fuel facility. These arrangements show layers of delivery capability and an institutional operator. They do not reveal tank contents, usable jet fuel, replenishment lead time or days of cover. A resilience assessment should test the whole delivery chain and backup activation, rather than label a facility a single point of failure without evidence. [",
