  "Can an airline improve energy security by buying fuel somewhere else? Fuel tankering means carrying additional fuel from an origin airport to reduce purchases later. The same action can respond to price differences or an interruption in supply. This project asks what destination price premium compensates the additional fuel consumed in transport, and how much destination refuelling demand a given extra uplift can displace. Its contribution is a reproducible threshold model linked to an East Asian policy comparison. It evaluates conditional trade-offs rather than claiming to identify profitable trades from unavailable airport prices.": {
    "en": "Can an airline improve energy security by buying fuel somewhere else? Fuel tankering means carrying additional fuel from an origin airport to reduce purchases later. The same action can respond to price differences or an interruption in supply. This project asks what destination price premium compensates the additional fuel consumed in transport, and how much destination refuelling demand a given extra uplift can displace. Its contribution is a reproducible threshold model linked to an East Asian policy comparison. It evaluates conditional trade-offs rather than claiming to identify profitable trades from unavailable airport prices.",
    "zh": "航空公司能否通过换一个地方买油来改善能源安全？提前携油，是指在出发机场多带一些燃油，减少后续机场的采购。这既可以应对价格差异，也可以应对供油中断。本项目研究两个问题：目的地价格需要高出多少，才能补偿运输燃油本身造成的额外耗油；给定额外加油量，又能替代多少目的地加油需求。研究将可复现的临界价差模型与东亚政策比较结合起来，分析在明确条件下的取舍。由于机场成交价尚未取得，本文不据此认定某条航线存在实际套利机会。"
  },
  "The question matters because Asian aviation connects globally traded oil to infrastructure that must deliver a specific product at a specific time. EIA estimates that Asia received 89% of crude oil and condensate passing through Hormuz in the first half of 2025; this is not a measurement of jet fuel deliveries. The IEA's 2026 Southeast Asia outlook also identifies dependence on Middle Eastern crude and constraints on substituting refinery feedstocks. These sources establish exposure, not the probability that Changi, Hong Kong or Narita will run short. A national oil inventory cannot automatically become certified jet fuel at an airport hydrant. [": {
    "en": "The question matters because Asian aviation connects globally traded oil to infrastructure that must deliver a specific product at a specific time. EIA estimates that Asia received 89% of crude oil and condensate passing through Hormuz in the first half of 2025; this is not a measurement of jet fuel deliveries. The IEA's 2026 Southeast Asia outlook also identifies dependence on Middle Eastern crude and constraints on substituting refinery feedstocks. These sources establish exposure, not the probability that Changi, Hong Kong or Narita will run short. A national oil inventory cannot automatically become certified jet fuel at an airport hydrant. [",
    "zh": "这个问题的重要性在于，亚洲航空业把全球石油贸易与必须按时交付特定产品的基础设施连接起来。EIA 估计，2025 年上半年通过霍尔木兹海峡的原油和凝析油中，有 89% 流向亚洲；这一数字描述的是上游石油流量。IEA 的《2026 年东南亚能源展望》也指出，中东原油依赖和炼厂原料替代存在约束。这些资料说明了暴露程度，但不能直接给出樟宜、香港或成田缺油的概率。国家石油储备要转变为可在机场地井交付的合格航油，还需要炼制、运输和供给权利。 ["
  },
