  "The model compares buying one tonne at the destination with loading enough additional fuel at the origin to deliver that same tonne. Route, payload, reserves, onward requirements and terminal fuel position are held constant. ICAO reports an aircraft-dependent additional fuel penalty of 2.5–4.5% of added weight per flight hour. I use that range as a sensitivity parameter, with 3.5% as an illustrative midpoint. A linear retention rule is the main approximation; an exponential rule tests structural sensitivity. Neither is an ICAO-prescribed equation or an aircraft performance calibration. Combustion emissions use ICAO's factor of 3.16 tonnes of CO₂ per tonne of Jet A fuel. [": {
    "en": "The model compares buying one tonne at the destination with loading enough additional fuel at the origin to deliver that same tonne. Route, payload, reserves, onward requirements and terminal fuel position are held constant. ICAO reports an aircraft-dependent additional fuel penalty of 2.5–4.5% of added weight per flight hour. I use that range as a sensitivity parameter, with 3.5% as an illustrative midpoint. A linear retention rule is the main approximation; an exponential rule tests structural sensitivity. Neither is an ICAO-prescribed equation or an aircraft performance calibration. Combustion emissions use ICAO's factor of 3.16 tonnes of CO₂ per tonne of Jet A fuel. [",
    "zh": "模型比较两种方式：在目的地购买 1 吨燃油，或在出发地额外装载足够燃油，使其中 1 吨抵达目的地。比较时保持航线、载荷、备份油、后续需求和终点油量一致。ICAO 文献给出的额外重量耗油范围为每飞行小时 2.5–4.5%，具体数值因飞机而异。本文将这一范围用于敏感性分析，以 3.5% 作为示例中点。主模型采用线性剩余比例，指数形式用于检验模型结构的影响。二者均为本文采用的近似，而非 ICAO 指定公式或机型性能标定。燃烧排放采用 ICAO 的换算系数，即每吨 Jet A 燃油对应 3.16 吨 CO₂。 ["
  },
